            <ArticleTitle>[Bilateral synalgias].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>631-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Total pulpitis leads in most cases to unilateral synalgia. Bilateral synalgiae are considerably rarer, but theoretically possible, in which pain radiates to the non-affected half of the jaw or face. Case reports illustrate the symptomatology, cause and therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
